Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: expose the existing FLAC decoder to Media Foundation

FFmpeg already decodes FLAC and the demux source already publishes its RIFF
subtype with STREAMINFO as codec user data. The generic Wine audio MFT is
neither registered for that subtype nor willing to accept it, so a valid
FLAC source cannot resolve a playable topology. P5's FLAC HLS test discovers
audio but never reaches CANPLAY.

Add FLAC to the two existing tables. Keep format conversion, codec data,
channel/rate bounds, resampling, output negotiation and flush unchanged.
The existing RIFF codec lookup maps WAVE_FORMAT_FLAC to AV_CODEC_ID_FLAC;
no additional decoder, container implementation or private GUID is needed.

This admits source-shaped FLAC with codec data. It does not relax the shared
minimum codec-data check, add inline-header-only MF input, claim arbitrary
channel masks, or fix missing topology-error forwarding. Float output can
represent 16/24-bit PCM; actual preservation requires the decode tests, and
32-bit lossless output is not claimed.
---
diff --git a/dlls/msauddecmft/msauddecmft.c b/dlls/msauddecmft/msauddecmft.c
--- a/dlls/msauddecmft/msauddecmft.c
+++ b/dlls/msauddecmft/msauddecmft.c
@@ -127,6 +127,7 @@
         {MFMediaType_Audio, MFAudioFormat_Vorbis},
         {MFMediaType_Audio, MFAudioFormat_Opus},
         {MFMediaType_Audio, MFAudioFormat_ADPCM},
+        {MFMediaType_Audio, MFAudioFormat_FLAC},
     };
     MFT_REGISTER_TYPE_INFO audio_decoder_mft_outputs[] =
     {
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/audio_decoder.c b/dlls/winedmo/audio_decoder.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/audio_decoder.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/audio_decoder.c
@@ -836,6 +836,7 @@
     {.Format = {.wFormatTag = WAVE_FORMAT_OPUS, .nChannels = 6, .nSamplesPerSec = 48000, .nAvgBytesPerSec = 1152000,
                 .nBlockAlign = 24, .wBitsPerSample = 32, .cbSize = sizeof(WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE) - sizeof(WAVEFORMATEX)}},
     {.Format = {.wFormatTag = WAVE_FORMAT_ADPCM, .cbSize = sizeof(WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE) - sizeof(WAVEFORMATEX)}},
+    {.Format = {.wFormatTag = WAVE_FORMAT_FLAC, .cbSize = sizeof(WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE) - sizeof(WAVEFORMATEX)}},
     {.Format = {.wFormatTag = 0x0160, .cbSize = sizeof(WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE) - sizeof(WAVEFORMATEX)}},  /* WMA v1 */
     {.Format = {.wFormatTag = 0x0161, .cbSize = sizeof(WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE) - sizeof(WAVEFORMATEX)}},  /* WMA v2/v8 */
     {.Format = {.wFormatTag = 0x0162, .cbSize = sizeof(WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE) - sizeof(WAVEFORMATEX)}},  /* WMA Pro/v9 */
